    "note": "On a rail that starts from rest, the spatial period of a fixed pulse cycle, Lambda = v(t) * T, grows as speed grows. The number of periods actually laid equals the pulse count (approximately t/T). A uniform standing-wave mode uses one wavelength. Exit-speed spacing is longer than mean spacing, so fewer uniform exit-speed periods fit in L than pulses that were laid. That mismatch is the chirp."
